.TH SDL_getenv 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_getenv \- Get the value of a variable in the environment.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_getenv(const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The name of the variable is case sensitive on all platforms\[char46]
.PP
This function uses SDL\(aqs cached copy of the environment and is thread-safe\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I name
the name of the variable to get\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the value of the variable or NULL if it can\(aqt be found\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

